            <ArticleTitle>Visceral angioedema related to treatment with an ACE inhibitor.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>319-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>For more than five years, a patient suffered recurrent episodes of abdominal pain accompanied by diarrhoea, nausea and vomiting. An angiotensin converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitor causing visceral oedema was eventually implicated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
